g API change.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"work state index sourc cutoff 2026 02 27t17 20 46z final work state through 2026 03 11 sourc link scheme path are relat to the final handoff locat work registri work state opentelemetri in the curat packag resolv the same path via the opentelemetri work registri opentelemetri symlink no content rewrit at handoff item coverag primari refer work state index sourc cutoff 2026 02 27t17 20 46z final work state through 2026 03 11 sourc link scheme path are relat to the final handoff locat work registri work state opentelemetri in the curat packag resolv the same path via the opentelemetri work registri opentelemetri symlink no content rewrit at handoff key blocker and activ item activ open public of the complet local otelgin cleanup 5946 6609 otelconf rc experiment api track runtim profil follow up 8014 close without merg not done complet intern extern record pend otelgin removeal cleanup os fuzz maintain mail list trial monitor path merg but unreleas 7443 7474 move to v1 400 no v1 400 releas sourc block defer immut signatur releas enabl releas tool confirm otelgrpc stabil rpc semconv grpc engag public os fuzz github auto file larg runtim profil api chang\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"6e3e7c908da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"document_keyword\": \"work-states/index.md\", \"id\": \"2cf0729de98d1b0f\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.47179737396533006, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.3860296128076144, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67192215, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"work-states/index.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"6e3e7c908da711f18c2f6b4f6cd8a654\", \"name\": \"work-states/index.md\", \"location\": \"work-states/index.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 3423, \"chunk_count\": 3, \"create_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:27\", \"update_date\": \"2026-08-01T20:49:43\", \"token_count\": 1309, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"work-state-index\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: [SRC-NOTE-04]\\n\\n# Meeting Note: OpenTelemetry Go SIG — 2025-11-03\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go/issues/6648#issuecomment-3479584781  \\n\\n**Author**: pellared  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z · **Updated**: 2025-11-03T09:18:08Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Date:** 2025-10-16\\n\\n**Attendees:**\\n\\n*   Tyler Yahn\\n\\n*   Damien Mathieu\\n\\n*   Bryan Boreham\\n\\n*   David Ashpole\\n\\n*   Robert Pająk\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**1. otelgin Context Reversal in DataRace**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** raised an issue regarding context reversal in DataRace for otelgin. The context, stored within the otelgin struct, is reverted after middleware execution to prevent parent middlewares from accessing the span. However, Go routines spawned after a request might still need the span in their context. This discussion was based on [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014).\\n\\n*   Damien believes the current behavior is correct and that users should explicitly pass the current context to spawned Go routines. He cited the collector's pattern of passing context directly outside HTTP requests for processors and exporters as a good example.\\n\\n*   **Tyler Yahn** agreed, suggesting that passing necessary values like the span to spawned Go routines is the appropriate solution. He also mentioned OpenTelemetry's pattern of linking spans for asynchronous operations rather than making them child references.\\n\\n**2. otelgin Middleware and Temporary Multi-part Forms**\\n\\n*   **Damien Mathieu** brought up an issue where using middleware causes temporary multi-part forms not to be destroyed. This occurs because the instrumentation clones the HTTP request, but the multipart form is not duplicated, preventing proper cleanup. This issue is a historical one, manifesting in otelgin but potentially affecting virtually all HTTP-related middleware.\\n\\n*   References for this issue include:\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/issues/5946)\\n\\n    *   [https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/6609)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src note 04 meet note opentelemetri go sig 2025 11 03 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go issu 6648 issuecom 3479584781 author pellar creat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z updat 2025 11 03t09 18 08z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z date 2025 10 16 attende tyler yahn damien mathieu bryan boreham david ashpol robert paj ą k transcript 1 otelgin context revers in datarac damien mathieu rais an issu regard context revers in datarac for otelgin the context store within the otelgin struct is revert after middlewar execut to prevent parent middlewar from access the span howev go routin spawn after a request might still need the span in their context this discuss wa base on http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 damien belief the current behavior is correct and that user should explicit pas the current context to spawn go routin he cite the collector s pattern of pass context direct outsid http request for processor and export a a good exampl tyler yahn agre suggest that pass necessari valu like the span to spawn go routin is the appropri solut he also mention opentelemetri s pattern of link span for asynchron oper rather than make them child refer 2 otelgin middlewar and temporari multi part form damien mathieu brought up an issu where use middlewar caus temporari multi part form not to be destroy this occur becaus the instrument clone the http request but the multipart form is not duplic prevent proper cleanup this issu is a histor one manifest in otelgin but potenti affect virtual all http relat middlewar refer for this issu includ http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib issu 5946 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609 http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 6609\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"id\": \"42b509db2d6a0a72\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.40669919525041676, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.285627786072024, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68919915, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"073cfcdc8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/meeting-notes/entry-3479584781.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 8756, \"chunk_count\": 4, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:50:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:11:19\", \"token_count\": 2164, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  - Comment: Tyler and I settled over DM that otelgin will call `MultipartForm.RemoveAll()` automatically (not reattach, not leave cleanup to users). I finished conflict resolution and tests for `#6609` locally and treat the MultipartForm cleanup work as done. I have not pushed the final commits or updated `#5946` / `#6609` on GitHub yet.\\n\\n  - Evidenc