gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:49:47Z\\n\\n@dmathieu maybe we should discuss this in the SIG since it might have implications in the other instrumentation modules\\n\\n**dmathieu** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-14T17:50:46Z\\n\\nI won't be able to attend this week's meeting (it's the week where it's late for EU). But yes, feel free to bring it there.\\n\\n**akats7** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-19T18:17:34Z\\n\\n@Yiling-J what are you thoughts on parsing the form in the middleware, the more I think about it, the more that seems to be the better approach, for example what about certain edge cases where down the chain middlewares might want to access the files\\n\\n**Yiling-J** on `instrumentation/github.com/gin-gonic/gin/otelgin/gin.go` (line 109) — 2025-01-20T01:52:04Z\\n\\n@akats7 Another option is to save `c.Request` to a variable before calling `c.Request.WithContext(ctx)`. Then, in the defer function, if `c.Request.MultipartForm != nil`, we can reattach the `MultipartForm` to the original request. This way, there won’t be any automatic removing or parsing. If other middlewares handle the form correctly, this approach should work. \\n\\nIn [http/server.go](https://github.com/golang/go/blob/40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41/src/net/http/server.go#L2102), the `ServeHTTP` method is called first, which invokes the Gin handlers/middlewares, and then `finishRequest` is called, which removes the temporary files.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"i think this approach could work but it feel a bit unusu to enforc form pars in the middlewar dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t16 18 27z have to forc remov multipart file is a bit unusu too akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 44 13z i m probabl more in favor of do the initi on the origin request a well explicit handl clean up logic doe seem a bit strang akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 49 47z dmathieu mayb we should discus this in the sig sinc it might have implic in the other instrument modul dmathieu on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 14t17 50 46z i won t be abl to attend this week s meet it s the week where it s late for eu but yes feel free to bring it there akats7 on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 19t18 17 34z yile j what are you thought on pars the form in the middlewar the more i think about it the more that seem to be the better approach for exampl what about certain edg case where down the chain middlewar might want to access the file yile j on instrument github com gin gonic gin otelgin gin go line 109 2025 01 20t01 52 04z akats7 anoth option is to save c request to a variabl befor call c request withcontext ctx then in the defer function if c request multipartform nil we can reattach the multipartform to the origin request this way there won t be ani automat remov or pars if other middlewar handl the form correct this approach should work in http server go http github com golang go blob 40b3c0e58a0ae8dec4684a009bf3806769e0fc41 src net http server go l2102 the servehttp method is call first which invok the gin handler middlewar and then finishrequest is call which remov the temporari file\", \"dataset_id\": \"b5f5be0e8a9b11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"074e174c8a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-6609.md\", \"id\": \"5d9f24da375839b6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.35869964457352477, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.19532669224789254, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7399032, \"dataset_name\": \"С2WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib